HCF (Highest Common Factor) or GCD (Greatest Common Divisor) of two numbers is the largest number that divides both of them. 

For example, GCD of 20 and 28 is 4, and GCD of 98 and 56 is 14.

Recommended: Please solve it on “PRACTICE ” first, before moving on to the solution.  Approach 1:We have discussed the recursive solution in the below post. Recursive program to find GCD or HCF of two numbers

Below is the iterative implementation of Euclid's algorithm 



            C++

    // C++ program to find HCF of two
// numbers iteratively.
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int hcf(int a, int b)
{
    if (a == 0)
        return b;
    else if (b == 0)
        return a;
    while (a != b) {
        if (a > b)
            a = a - b;
        else
            b = b - a;
    }
    return a;
}

// Driver code
int main()
{
    int a = 60, b = 96;
    cout << hcf(a, b) << endl;
    return 0;
}

